course: dictionary
lesson: 261
title: Aluminium: a light metal that does not rust
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Aluminium is a metal, and it is light and silver-coloured. Words around it give you clues about what it does. «Big magnets pull out steel cans, while aluminium, which is not magnetic, is separated in other ways.» The words which is not magnetic tell you that a magnet will not pick up aluminium.
explain: Context helps you spot what a word names. «A drinks can starts as a flat disc of aluminium punched into a cup and stretched tall.» Here aluminium is the material the can is made from, so you can work out that aluminium is a metal used for making things.
explain: Ask yourself what the word is doing in the sentence. Is it a thing, an action or a describing word? Aluminium is a noun, so it names something: the metal itself. Then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Aluminium is a light, silver-coloured metal that does not rust.
fact: Aluminium is the metal used to make drink cans, foil, window frames and parts of planes.
fact: Aluminium is not magnetic, so a magnet does not pick it up.
fact: «An aluminium can can be recycled and be back on the shelf within about two months.»
fact: Melting old cans needs far less energy than making aluminium from rock.
exercise: «A drinks can starts as a flat disc of aluminium.» What is aluminium in this sentence? | *A metal | A kind of drink | A glowing blob of sand | A type of magnet
exercise: «Big magnets pull out steel cans, while aluminium, which is not magnetic, is separated in other ways.» Why do magnets not pull out aluminium? | Aluminium is too hot | Aluminium is made of sand | Magnets are too small | *Aluminium is not magnetic
exercise: Which of these is made from aluminium? | Wooden spoons | Paper bags | Glass jars | *Drink cans
test: What is aluminium? | A kind of plastic that floats | A liquid used in cooking | A heavy black rock | *A light, silver-coloured metal that does not rust
test: «In a sorting plant, a spinning magnet pushes aluminium cans off the belt even though aluminium is not magnetic.» What does this sentence show? | Magnets always pick up aluminium | Aluminium cans are sorted by sound | Spinning magnets are never used | *Aluminium cans can be sorted even though a magnet does not pick them up
exam: Why is recycling aluminium cans good? | It makes the cans heavier | It stops cans being made at all | *It saves energy, because melting old cans needs far less energy than making aluminium from rock | It turns cans into magnets
